    "result_text": "The full suite passes (38 tests, 0 failures). \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `contactPreference` derived field: `'EMAIL'` when an owner has an email present, otherwise `'PHONE'`.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a `contactPreference` property (read-only string enum `EMAIL`/`PHONE`) to the `Owner` schema, so the OpenAPI generator emits it on `OwnerDto` (as `OwnerDto.ContactPreferenceEnum`).\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added `@Mapping(target = \"contactPreference\", expression = \"java(contactPreference(owner))\")` on `toOwnerDto` plus a `contactPreference(Owner)` default method returning `EMAIL` when `getEmail()` is non-null/non-blank, else `PHONE`. This mirrors the existing derived-field pattern (`locality`, `membershipLevel`, `membershipNumber`) and follows the same \"email present\" check already used by `membershipLevel`.\n\nThe field is computed on read in the mapper, so it applies uniformly to the `GET /api/owners/{id}` response the tests exercise. Both new `Cp27Tests` cases pass, and the full suite (38 tests) stays green.",
